title: Revert caller-facing precompile errors with a reason

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The System and Storage builtins, the XCM precompile, and the vesting precompile now return
    `Error::Revert` for caller-facing failures. `Error::Error` remains the trap used when a
    precompile runs out of gas or hits a broken invariant. `From<DispatchError>` is unchanged, so
    a `?` on a dispatch error still traps. Map those errors at the call site.

    `pallet_revive::precompiles` now exports `ensure_not_delegate_call`, `ensure_not_read_only`,
    and the reasons `DELEGATE_CALL_DENIED` and `STATIC_CALL_DENIED`.
    `ensure_not_read_only` is the only place that decides whether a static call reverts or traps.
    `Error::try_to_revert` also maps `DispatchError::RootNotAllowed` to
    "root origin is not allowed", `EcdsaRecoveryFailed` to "invalid compressed public key",
    `ContractNotFound` to "no contract to terminate", and `DispatchError::Token` to the same
    sentences `From<TokenError> for &'static str` already uses. The delegate-call text is
    unchanged.

    No precompile signature change and no storage migration. A runtime that already registers
    these precompiles picks up the new reasons on upgrade. Nothing to reconfigure.

- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Contracts that call these precompiles should catch `Error(string)`. The failures below used
    to trap, so `catch Error(string)` did not run and the return data was empty. `eth_call` and
    tracers showed a revert with no reason.

    - `DELEGATECALL` to the XCM or vesting precompile now reverts.
    - A static call of XCM `send` or `execute`, a state-changing vesting method, System
      `terminate`, or Storage `clearStorage` / `takeStorage` now reverts.
    - System `ownCodeHash` for the root origin, and any vesting call whose caller is root, now
      reverts with "root origin is not allowed".
    - System `ecdsaToEthAddress` with a public key that is not a valid compressed secp256k1 key
      reverts with "invalid compressed public key".
    - System `terminate` called when there is no contract to destroy (an EOA calling the
      precompile directly) reverts with "no contract to terminate".
    - System `terminate` whose balance transfer fails with a token error reverts with that
      error's reason, for example "Funds exist but are frozen" or "Funds are unavailable".
    - Storage `takeStorage` reports the same write failure as `clearStorage`
    - XCM `send` and `execute` name the `pallet_xcm` error. A failed `execute` includes the
      instruction index, for example
      "XCM execute failed: local execution incomplete at instruction 3: FailedToTransactAsset".
    - Vesting `vest`, `vestOther`, and `vestedTransfer` name the pallet error.

    Running out of gas still traps with empty return data. No storage migration and no signature
    change. Update any caller that matched empty return data or one of the old generic strings.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-xcm-precompiles
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-vesting-precompiles
  bump: patch
